audio:
  lang: en
  lines:
    female|a||Without a lottery, can we still get a lottery's answer, by comparing insured and uninsured people who look the same on paper?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Picture three hundred adults on low incomes, and no lottery anywhere. The numbers are made up, to keep the idea plain.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8080
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:4tk96w'
    female|a||Two hundred of them have coverage. In the last thirty days they had fourteen good days of physical health, on average.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:qn5zyx'
    female|a||The hundred without coverage had twenty-two.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:mik8sz'
    female|a||Taken at face value, insurance costs eight good days a month.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:15aknos'
    female|a||Nobody believes that. Coverage is something people sign up for, and the sick have the most reason to.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14xpdc0'
    'female|a||So sort them first, by what the records show: how many chronic conditions each person has on file. Call that X.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:m3whkm'
    female|a||With none on file, twenty have signed up and eighty haven't.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1by6qvi'
    'female|a||With one condition it flips: eighty signed up, twenty didn''t.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:5enprr'
    female|a||And with two or more, all hundred are covered.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2wvdto'
    female|a||Before the numbers, a guess. Inside the row with no conditions on file, will the insured still look worse off than the uninsured?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17mdurm'
    'female|a||Better off: inside one row the sickness on file is the same for both sides, so it no longer drags the insured down.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Inside that row, the insured had twenty-six good days, and the uninsured twenty-four.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Among those with one condition, sixteen against fourteen.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1xgo0e'
    'female|a||Both rows tell the same story: coverage goes with two more good days, not eight fewer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t5x13h'
    female|a||The minus eight was never the insurance. It was the sick sorting themselves into coverage, and the rows have sorted them back.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ea8h0d'
    female|a||Comparing only people the records cannot tell apart is called matching.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mzlxuy'
    female|a||The bottom row has ten good days among the covered, and no one uninsured to compare them with. Hold on to that empty cell.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ypi2s8'
    female|a||But is plus two the effect of coverage? Only if one thing is true of the people inside each row.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:a55fwk'
    'female|a||What does matching assume, when it calls that plus two an effect? Look inside one row: people with one condition on file.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Eighty of them are insured, and we see their sixteen good days, their life with coverage.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:xzxape'
    female|a||Their life without coverage never happened. It is a blank.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 3760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1b3h2rx'
    'female|a||For the twenty uninsured it''s the other way round: we see fourteen, and their covered life is the blank.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1q6tydr'
    female|a||Matching fills the insured's blank with their neighbours' fourteen.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10dh6he'
    'female|a||That is where plus two comes from: sixteen, minus a borrowed fourteen.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1j0n839'
    'female|a||The borrowing is the whole assumption. Write D for coverage, one for covered: had they stayed uninsured, the insured would have done just as well as the uninsured beside them.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fn79s8'
    'female|a||Economists ask a little more, and write it with a bar: once you know X, coverage says nothing about either potential future. They call it conditional independence.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jvcbo2'
    female|a||A lottery hands you the same line without the bar, because a draw cannot see anyone's health.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1jffu3g'
    female|a||The bar is the leap of faith. It says that everything that sent people into coverage is written in the row label.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1v4iwkz'
    'female|a||So what must be true of the twenty uninsured? That they stayed out for reasons unrelated to their health: a lost form, a clinic that never mentioned it.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1czo34c'
    female|a||Now suppose many of the eighty signed up because they'd felt unwell for months, and no doctor had written it down.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sura68'
    female|a||Then their blank isn't fourteen. On average, say it's twelve.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:133vt0e'
    'female|a||Their true gain is sixteen minus twelve: four good days, not two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:14dkv0t'
    female|a||And nothing in the data warns you. The numbers you can see are exactly the same either way.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8zxxb1'
    'female|a||That is what conditional independence asserts: not something about your records, but about the people your records cannot tell apart.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:owy8ke'
    female|a||Back to the row where everyone is covered. What happens to people who have no one to be compared with?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6640
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Shade each row by who has coverage: a fifth of the first row,':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5280
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sb8rpf'
    female|a||four fifths of the second,:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1n5lsln'
    female|a||and every single person in the third.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2720
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:utamry'
    'female|a||That share is the propensity score: the chance of coverage, given what''s on file.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6200
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10dcwuc'
    female|a||Rosenbaum and Rubin showed in 1983 that people with the same score are balanced on everything on file, so one number can stand in for a long list.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:fk6o3o'
    female|a||But a comparison needs both kinds of person at each score, so the score must lie strictly between zero and one. That is common support.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9560
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:nsud3j'
    female|a||That is for the effect on everyone. For the effect on the insured, the score need only stay below one, and the third row fails even that.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1p8dfsg'
    female|a||With a score of one, there is no uninsured neighbour to borrow from, so the blank can't be filled, only guessed.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:qa28c3'
    female|a||So matching drops the row.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 2440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mbzgag'
    female|a||With the third row dropped, whose effect does the plus two now describe?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:pk7byw'
    'female|a||The first two rows: the hundred people in the third row have left the question, not just the data.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6080
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Plus two now speaks for two hundred people, not the three hundred we set out to study.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5560
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||Ask about the people who have coverage, and it''s worse: half of the two hundred insured sat in the dropped row.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1enusml'
    female|a||They're the sickest, where coverage might matter most, and the estimate is silent about them.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:oje94f'
    female|a||Nothing in the output flags it. The number arrives with a tidy standard error, for a smaller group than the one you meant.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:l4oykd'
    female|a||Real scores rarely hit zero or one exactly, so a common rule, from Crump, Hotz, Imbens and Mitnik, keeps only scores between point one and point nine.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 11880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:vhlm6t'
    female|a||Trimming is honest about what the data can say. But every person it drops changes the question, so say whom the answer is about.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9520
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:8s7qux'
    female|a||Matching is one way to fill the blanks; regression is another, and it comes in more than one kind. Put the rows on a chart to see.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 8600
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||The insured, in blue: twenty-six good days, sixteen, and ten, as conditions pile up.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6400
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:arc44u'
    'female|a||The uninsured, in red: twenty-four and fourteen, and nobody at all with two or more.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:19j372b'
    'female|a||Matching compares straight up, inside each row: plus two, and plus two.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 5600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1aq4mt9'
    female|a||At two or more conditions it stops. There is no one to compare with, so it says nothing.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6360
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:jtcdqa'
    female|a||One kind of regression doesn't stop. Fit a line to the uninsured, and use it to predict their blanks.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:lu213k'
    female|a||At two or more conditions, the line predicts four good days for the uninsured.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5760
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1gr6d59'
    'female|a||So coverage would be worth six there: a number read off a ruler, not off people.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:17e05k5'
    'female|a||If the sickest would have done better or worse than a straight line, six is wrong, and nothing in the data can say so. That is where matching beats a prediction: it won''t invent a blank with no neighbours.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:psq2i9'
    'female|a||The regression most people run is a different thing: good days on coverage, with a dummy for each row as the control.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 7600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1fcl4ic'
    'female|a||It weighs each row by its size times p times one minus p: sixteen, sixteen, and zero for the row where everyone is covered.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 9600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:gk7g7l'
    female|a||So it lands on plus two, and quietly drops the full-coverage row, just as matching does.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:11a3t4q'
    'female|a||Matching for the insured weighs the rows by how many insured they hold: twenty and eighty.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6440
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:2nwup7'
    female|a||Here the gain is two in every row, so the weights don't matter. When the gain differs from row to row, they move the number, often only a little.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10160
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1lsv8u9'
    female|a||Put the conditions in as one straight line instead, and regression says about one point two, because a straight line fits the insured badly too.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9040
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1mgggkz'
    'female|a||Regression has real gifts: it uses everyone, handles dozens of controls at once, and gives a standard error almost for free. But look at what every version used as the insured''s life without coverage: the same red dots.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 15600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1s7iduw'
    female|a||If those dots are the wrong stand-in, matching and every regression are wrong together, and in the same direction.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7320
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1sf79x'
    'female|a||How wrong can that stand-in be? Across: how much sicker the insured are than their uninsured twins, in ways no record shows.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 8880
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||Matching, and a regression with a dummy for each row, both read plus two, whatever that hidden gap is, because the data they see do not change.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1pw7gtw'
    female|a||The true effect is plus two only where the gap is zero. It climbs one day for every day of hidden gap.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 7480
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ylhc71'
    female|a||Watch the point move toward insured people who were secretly sicker, and see which line follows it.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6600
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1hplrp4'
    'female|a||The truth climbs away, while both estimates sit still: neither method can see it move.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 6520
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    female|a||At a hidden gap of two, the case of the eighty in the one-condition row, on average, coverage is worth four, and both methods say two.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 10640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:laceku'
    female|a||Does this happen with real people? Oregon offers a check.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 4120
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1ohqubx'
    'female|a||In two thousand and eight, Oregon held a lottery for Medicaid: about ninety thousand low-income adults signed up, and about thirty thousand names were drawn. Chance, not health, decided who got the offer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13000
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:10dhnon'
    'female|a||Its researchers set their result beside national surveys of adults below the poverty line, which ask the same question: on how many of the last thirty days was your physical health good?':
      mp3: 
      ms: 11840
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:12qqpis'
    female|a||In those surveys, the insured reported about two and a quarter good days fewer than the uninsured.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 6880
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1g9nm11'
    female|a||Control for age, sex, race, schooling, marriage, children, work and income, and the gap shrinks to about one day fewer.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9240
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:uw78ys'
    female|a||Where did Oregon's lottery put the effect of Medicaid on the same measure? Click the line.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 5800
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:j3oin9'
    female|a||Plus one and a third, give or take about one point one. The controls moved the estimate the right way, but never across zero.:
      mp3: 
      ms: 9800
      voice: gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed
    'female|a||These are different people in different years, so it is a rough benchmark. The researchers read the gap as selection: among people on low incomes, those who take up coverage are sicker, just like our row.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 13680
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:bbi9n4'
    'female|a||Defenders of matching answer that richer records, years of claims and diagnoses, would close the gap. The way to find out is exactly this: run the method where a lottery already knows the answer.':
      mp3: 
      ms: 12920
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:t9j7tv'
    female|a||One new case. A clinic offers free diet coaching. Researchers compare patients who joined with non-joiners who match them on age, weight and diagnoses. What would most bias the result?:
      mp3: 
      ms: 13640
      voice: 'gemini:Achird | clear, warm economist who thinks aloud and explains with care; steady, lively pace, just a touch slower than brisk; never slow, never rushed #ctx:1t2h0mz'
    female|a||Their resolve is in no record, so the matched non-joiners are a poor stand-in for what the joiners would have done anyway.:
